      <div type="clause" n="27">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 27</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="27" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXI.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.24"/> Se ðe dearnenga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.25"/> bearn gestrieneð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.26"/> ⁊ gehileð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.27"/>, nah se his deaðes wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.28"/>, ac his hlaford ⁊ se cyning.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.29"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="27" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXI. Se ðe dearnunga bearn gestrynð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.8"/> ⁊ geheleþ, nah se his deaþes wer, ac his hlaford ⁊ se cyning.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="27" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe dearnunge bearn stryneð. Se ðe dearnunga bearn gestreonað ⁊ geheleð, nah se his deaðes wér, ac his hlaford ⁊ se cyng.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="27" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="101" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui in occulto puerum genuerit et celabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.21"/>, non habeat ipsius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.22"/> pueri weram, si occidatur, sed rex et dominus suus.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_27.lnote.oe.23"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="44" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam þe dearnunge bearn stryneð.] Se ðe dearnenga bearn gestrieneð ⁊ gehileð, nah se his deaðes wer, ac his hlaford ⁊ se cyning.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="27" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="392" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXI} Se ðe dearnenga bearn gestrieneð ⁊ gehileð, nah se his deaðes wer, ac his hlaford ⁊ se cyning.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="101" ed="#liebermann"/>Wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_27.lnote.de.1"/> unehelich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_27.lnote.de.2"/> ein Kind zeugt und nicht anerkennt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_27.lnote.de.3"/>, erhält das Wergeld von dessen Tödtung nicht, sondern der Herr [des Unehelichen] und der König.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whoever begets a child out of wedlock and does not acknowledge it does not receive the wergeld for its killing, but the lord [of the illegitimate child] and the king do.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="45" ed="#attenborough"/>He who begets an illegitimate child and disowns it shall not have the wergeld at its death, but its lord and<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_27.attnote.n.1"/> the king shall [have it].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="402" ed="#whitelock"/>Whoever begets an illegitimate child and does not acknowledge it, has no right to the wergild at its death, but its lord and the king [have it].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="393" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>He who conceives a child out of wedlock and hides it – he will not have its <hi rend="italic">wer</hi> upon its death, but [it goes to] his lord and the king.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="393"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_23-1">Ine 23.1</ref> <quote>but compare §22.1.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="229"><ref target="clause:Af_El-to-6">Af El 6</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">celauerit <hi rend="italic">Br Hn</hi> 78, 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">celauerit Br Hn 78, 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">p. i. <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br;</hi> cognatio illius <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">p. i. M Hk Br; cognatio illius Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K; übergeschr. Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K; written above Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">yn:ð <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">yn:ð on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">28; 28, 1.2 <hi rend="italic">stellt vor</hi> 27 <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ld places 28; 28, 1.2 before 27</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">deornunga <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">deornunga Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gestreonaþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gestreonaþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">geheleþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">geheleþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">were <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">were Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyng <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyng Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diesen Satz benutzt Hn 78, 4. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Bastard 1; Sippe 9; König 14; Gefolge 22</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hn 78, 4 makes use of this sentence. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Bastard 1; Sippe 9; König 14; Gefolge 22</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So, nicht ‘heimlich’; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> S. 41 zur Rb</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So, not ‘secretly’; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> p. 41 on the Rb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_27.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> auch Brunner <hi rend="italic">Ausserehel. Vaterschaft</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Savigny Zs. Rg.</hi> 17 (1896) 15. — Vermutlich heisst ‘und’ in letzter Zeile: ‘beziehungsweise, oder’, nämlich wenn kein Herr vorhanden [und keine Gilde; Ine 21] zum Einklagen des Wergeldes für den erschlagenen Bastard</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> also Brunner <hi rend="italic">Ausserehel. Vaterschaft</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Savigny Zs. Rg.</hi> 17 (1896) 15. — ‘And’ in the last line presumably means ‘respectively, or’, namely when there is no lord [and no gild; Ine 21] to sue for the wergild for the slain bastard</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_27.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann suggests that <hi rend="italic">and</hi> should be translated ‘or,’ and that the king obtains the wergeld when there is no lord. It is possible, however, that the intention is to divide the sum, as in cap. 23 § 1, where (as against Liebermann’s view) <hi rend="italic">se gesið</hi> may correspond to <hi rend="italic">his hlaford</hi> here (cf. also note 1 to cap. 50 below).</seg></note>
      </div>
